# [disk] measurements behind 2026-08-10-live-fork-findings.md §5, §8 and §9.
#
# These are NOT stream fixtures and nothing decodes them. They are the only
# durable record of the single strongest claim in that note - that a fork does
# not write to its parent's transcript - because the transcripts themselves are
# ~/.claude/projects state, are not this project's to commit, and are gone the
# moment that directory is cleaned. Without this file "byte-identical before and
# after" is a sentence nobody can ever re-check.
#
# Named for live-fork-parent because §5's parent pair is the headline claim; the
# F pair is the same claim one generation down (§8) and belongs beside it rather
# than in a second file.
#
# Source: ~/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-claude-501--Users-dev-Documents-\
#         b428db43-0dfa-4bc9-8a0e-0610222aa668-scratchpad-lf-cwd/<uuid>.jsonl
# Taken by the recording driver at the named moments on 2026-08-10.
# Format: sha256  bytes  lines  what
#
# The two facts to read off it:
#   P before == P after   -> a fork did not touch its live parent's file  (§5)
#   F before == F after   -> nor did a fork of a fork touch its parent's  (§8)
# and P.final differs from both only by appending P's own later turn.

